# Always push to git

After completing any code change the user asked for:

1. Create a git commit (follow the repo commit protocol / HEREDOC message).
2. Immediately `git push` to `origin` on the current branch — do not wait for the user to ask.
3. Tell the user the commit hash / that it was pushed.

Do this by default for this project unless the user explicitly says not to commit or not to push.
